@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Logical runtime DFD — data meaning, not control order
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

rectangle "E1 Authorized caller context" as U
usecase "P1\nValidate / admit owned intent" as P1
database "D1 Owned records / command / pending intent" as D1
usecase "P2\nResolve eligible scoped attempt" as P2
rectangle "E2 External facility" as E
usecase "P3\nInterpret actual observation" as P3
database "D2 Attempt / effect evidence" as D2
usecase "P4\nProject permitted outcome" as P4
U --> P1 : command identity / resource / versions / input
P1 --> D1 : guarded record / result / pending intent data
D1 --> P2 : exact committed attempt context
P2 --> E : scoped external request data
E --> P3 : response / actual observation data
P3 --> D2 : confirmed / partial / unknown evidence
D1 --> P4 : local result / revision
D2 --> P4 : attributable effect knowledge
P4 --> U : permitted operation status / result
legend bottom
 E = external entity; P = transformation; D = logical data store (not mandatory separate databases).
 Arrows are data flows, not automatic triggers, transaction atomicity or granted permission.
 All transformations preserve current required scope and safe disclosure.
endlegend
@enduml
